 "summary": "Nothing in Mathlib or TauCeti covers derivative-sign order-convexity, Thom root encodings, or the 0/1 sign-count reconstruction; the PR consumes the existing PolynomialRolle, occCount/signCount, and fullInverse/Tarski-query APIs instead of re-deriving them. The Fin-indexed layer is required by the Fintype-indexed counting API and is derived from the \u2115-indexed layer via the single helper `derivativeSign_tail`, so it is not a parallel API.",
